  "ingredients": [
    "1 3/4 cup mozzarella cheese (shredded)",
    "1 ounce cream cheese (softened)",
    "3/4 cup almond flour",
    "1 large egg",
    "8 whole mozzarella cheese stick",
    "1/2 cup pork rinds (crushed)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 400F. Grate the mozzarella cheese that is listed first.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl, add the cream cheese, almond flour, and grated mozzarella. Microwave on high for about 30 seconds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the egg, then mix everything together. I like to use a silicone spatula, because it doesn't stick to the dough.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the dough on a piece of parchment or wax paper. If the dough is acting a bit \"wet\" and hard to handle, wax paper seems to work better.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place a second piece of paper on the top, then roll it out into a rectangular shape. Remove the top piece of paper and cut the rectangle into 8 smaller rectangles.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wrap the pieces of dough around the cheese sticks. You'll have to kind of mold the dough around them and even roll it on the table a little to get the perfect shape.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll the cheese sticks in the crushed pork rinds, pressing the rinds into the dough enough so that they stick without losing their shape. Place on a lined baking sheet.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20-25 minutes. They will look browned and spread out on the tray a bit. If you want them to be shaped more like mozzarella sticks, you can freeze them for 30 minutes first. Once frozen, you can bake or try deep frying them.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/mozzarella-cheese-pockets-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve with Ruled.me ketchup or marinara sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/mozzarella-cheese-pockets/#wprm-recipe-52491-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
